msgid "Simplified queries"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Normally, MongoDB queries are of this form: `{'firstname': 'John', "
"'lastname':'Doe'}`, this is what we call MongoDB native queries."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can use them if you want, but we also support what we call **PanacheQL** "
"that can be seen as a subset of link:https://docs.oracle.com/javaee/7/"
"tutorial/persistence-querylanguage.htm#BNBTG[JPQL] (or link:{hibernate-orm-"
"docs-url}#hql[HQL]) and allows you to easily express a query.\n"
"MongoDB with Panache will then map it to a MongoDB native query."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If your query does not start with `{`, we will consider it a PanacheQL query:"
""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`<singlePropertyName>` (and single parameter) which will expand to "
"`{'singleColumnName': '?1'}`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`<query>` will expand to `{<query>}` where we will map the PanacheQL query "
"to MongoDB native query form. We support the following operators that will "
"be mapped to the corresponding MongoDB operators: 'and', 'or' ( mixing 'and' "
"and 'or' is not currently supported), '=', '>', '>=', '<', '<=', '!=', 'is "
"null', 'is not null', and 'like' that is mapped to the MongoDB `$regex` "
"operator (both String and JavaScript patterns are supported)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Here are some query examples:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`firstname = ?1 and status = ?2` will be mapped to `{'firstname': ?1, "
"'status': ?2}`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`amount > ?1 and firstname != ?2` will be mapped to `{'amount': {'$gt': ?1}, "
"'firstname': {'$ne': ?2}}`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`lastname like ?1` will be mapped to `{'lastname': {'$regex': ?1}}`. Be "
"careful that this will be link:https://docs.mongodb.com/manual/reference/"
"operator/query/regex/#op._S_regex[MongoDB regex] support and not SQL like "
"pattern."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`lastname is not null` will be mapped to `{'lastname':{'$exists': true}}`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`status in ?1` will be mapped to `{'status':{$in: ?1}}`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We also handle some basic date type transformations: all fields of type "
"`Date`, `LocalDate`, `LocalDateTime` or `Instant` will be mapped to the\n"
"link:https://docs.mongodb.com/manual/reference/bson-types/#date[BSON Date] "
"using the `ISODate` type (UTC datetime).\n"
"The MongoDB POJO codec doesn't support `ZonedDateTime` and `OffsetDateTime` "
"so you should convert them prior usage."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"MongoDB with Panache also supports extended MongoDB queries by providing a "
"`Document` query, this is supported by the find/list/stream/count/delete/"
"update methods."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"MongoDB with Panache offers operations to update multiple documents based on "
"an update document and a query :\n"
"`Person.update(\"foo = ?1 and bar = ?2\", fooName, barName).where(\"name = "
"?1\", name)`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For these operations, you can express the update document the same way you "
"express your queries, here are some examples:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`<singlePropertyName>` (and single parameter) which will expand to the "
"update document `{'$set' : {'singleColumnName': '?1'}}`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`firstname = ?1 and status = ?2` will be mapped to the update document "
"`{'$set' : {'firstname': ?1, 'status': ?2}}`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`firstname = :firstname and status = :status` will be mapped to the update "
"document `{'$set' : {'firstname': :firstname, 'status': :status}}`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`{'firstname' : ?1 and 'status' : ?2}` will be mapped to the update document "
"`{'$set' : {'firstname': ?1, 'status': ?2}}`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`{'firstname' : :firstname and 'status' : :status}` will be mapped to the "
"update document `{'$set' : {'firstname': :firstname, 'status': :status}}`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`{'$inc': {'cpt': ?1}}` will be used as-is"
msgstr ""

